import{_ as i,o as t,c as o,a2 as a}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const m=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Entry 870 | Transcended Ones and Society | The Transcended One's Relationship with Mid-Level Cultivators","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 870 | Transcended Ones and Society | The Transcended One's Relationship with Mid-Level Cultivators","no":870,"module":4,"tags":["Transcendence","Society","Mid-Level Cultivators","Class Mobility","Myriad-Rank Republicanism"],"related":["36-Social Structure and Class Mobility","14-Unified Cultivation-Realm Classification","22-Resource Allocation Household-Responsibility Mechanism","872-Transcended One's Promotion of Social Mobility"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0870_模块4-超脱者与社会-超脱者与中产修炼者的关系.md","filePath":"en/0870_模块4-超脱者与社会-超脱者与中产修炼者的关系.md"}`),n={name:"en/0870_模块4-超脱者与社会-超脱者与中产修炼者的关系.md"};function s(r,e,l,d,h,c){return t(),o("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[a('<h1 id="entry-870-transcended-ones-and-society-the-transcended-one-s-relationship-with-mid-level-cultivators" tabindex="-1">Entry 870 | Transcended Ones and Society | The Transcended One&#39;s Relationship with Mid-Level Cultivators <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-870-transcended-ones-and-society-the-transcended-one-s-relationship-with-mid-level-cultivators" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 870 | Transcended Ones and Society | The Transcended One&#39;s Relationship with Mid-Level Cultivators&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 4 · Transcendence Orthodox Definition Library | Benchmark base: Documents 36, 14, 22, 872</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-mid-level-cultivators-are-civilization-s-waist-—-the-transcended-one-may-not-press-the-waist" tabindex="-1">Introduction: mid-level cultivators are civilization&#39;s waist — the transcended one may not press the waist <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-mid-level-cultivators-are-civilization-s-waist-—-the-transcended-one-may-not-press-the-waist" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: mid-level cultivators are civilization&#39;s waist — the transcended one may not press the waist&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The old world&#39;s cultivation society is a pyramid: the top is the Great Emperor; the middle is sect elders and family strong ones; the bottom is billions of mortals. This pyramid&#39;s waist — those cultivators with some cultivation far from the top — is the group most easily overlooked and most easily sacrificed. Heng Yuan Zhou must make clear: <strong>mid-level cultivators (roughly corresponding to the Transform Realm through Dao Integration Realm range) are civilization&#39;s waist; the transcended one&#39;s attitude toward them directly determines whether civilization is mobile or solidified.</strong> This entry explains this relationship.</p><p>Six top-level axioms simultaneously take the stage: the anti-predation axiom forbids the transcended one treating mid-level cultivators as &quot;harvestable leeks&quot;; the republican axiom of Myriad Races confirms mid-level cultivators are Myriad Ranks&#39; evolutionary backbone; the collective ascension axiom requires the transcended one lift mid-level cultivators upward, not press down on them; the causal self-discipline axiom requires the transcended one&#39;s resource allocation with mid-level cultivators be traceable; the law-first axiom requires the class-mobility mechanism be law-level self-consistent; the universal equal infinite law confirms all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; easygoing layabouts retain a floor and are not eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes may superimpose higher infinity — infinite origin is inherent in all, predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><p>The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-who-are-mid-level-cultivators" tabindex="-1">I. Who Are Mid-Level Cultivators <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-who-are-mid-level-cultivators" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Who Are Mid-Level Cultivators&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Per Unified Cultivation-Realm Classification (Document 14), mid-level cultivators roughly correspond to the Transform, Law, Dao Origin, and Dao Integration ranges — they have passed early mortal cultivation, have considerable cultivation and social-contribution capability, but are far from the Boundary-Breaking and above sage-cultivator level.</p><p>They are:</p><ul><li>Sect backbone lecturers, workshop master technicians, city enforcers;</li><li>Cultivation academy upper-grade students, cross-plane exploration team captains;</li><li>Technical backbone in every industry, primary bearers of grassroots governance.</li></ul><p>Civilization&#39;s daily operation relies not on the tower-top transcended one, but these waists. Waist hard → civilization stable; waist broken → civilization topples.</p><h2 id="ii-the-old-world-s-two-harms-to-mid-level-cultivators" tabindex="-1">II. The Old World&#39;s Two Harms to Mid-Level Cultivators <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-the-old-world-s-two-harms-to-mid-level-cultivators" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. The Old World&#39;s Two Harms to Mid-Level Cultivators&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The old world has two systematic harms to mid-level cultivators:</p><ol><li><strong>Harvest type</strong>: tower-top strong ones treat mid-level cultivators as &quot;harvestable middle resources&quot; — send them to die, make them take the blame, ambush them during breakthrough to snatch treasures. Mid-level cultivators have barely climbed halfway up the mountain; one word from a tower-top strong one wipes it all out.</li><li><strong>Suppression type</strong>: tower-top strong ones deliberately lock the ceiling halfway up, letting mid-level cultivators never reach the top. Because if too many people come up, tower-top power dilutes. Thus &quot;poor families rarely produce noble sons&quot; becomes &quot;the middle rarely produces strong ones.&quot;</li></ol><p>Both harms&#39; essence is the same: <strong>the tower top treats the middle as threat, not as echelon.</strong></p><h2 id="iii-heng-yuan-zhou-s-positive-relationship-echelon-relationship" tabindex="-1">III. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s Positive Relationship: Echelon Relationship <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-heng-yuan-zhou-s-positive-relationship-echelon-relationship" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s Positive Relationship: Echelon Relationship&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Heng Yuan Zhou defines the transcended one&#39;s relationship with mid-level cultivators as &quot;echelon&quot; — the transcended one is not a ceiling pressing on their heads, but a guide standing before them:</p><ul><li><strong>No harvest</strong>: mid-level cultivators&#39; breakthrough results belong to themselves; the transcended one intercepts in no form;</li><li><strong>No limitation</strong>: the ceiling is open to all; mid-level cultivators may go upward once qualified; the transcended one does not set limits by person;</li><li><strong>Give resources</strong>: the household-responsibility mechanism (Document 22) ensures mid-level cultivators&#39; labor receives reasonable return, no need to &quot;hand up to the sect&quot; or &quot;present tribute to elders&quot;;</li><li><strong>Give channels</strong>: cultivators at Dao Origin and Dao Integration stages may through the transcended-one training and transmission post (entry 720) receive one-on-one guidance, entering the preparation channel for Boundary-Breaking.</li></ul><p>The echelon relationship&#39;s core is: <strong>the transcended one treats mid-level cultivators as future transcended-one reserve, not as consumable supplies.</strong> Today&#39;s mid-level cultivator is tomorrow&#39;s post officeholder.</p><h2 id="iv-how-the-transcended-one-avoids-middle-solidification" tabindex="-1">IV. How the Transcended One Avoids &quot;Middle Solidification&quot; <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-how-the-transcended-one-avoids-middle-solidification" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. How the Transcended One Avoids &quot;Middle Solidification&quot;&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The greatest risk of class solidification comes from the transcended one himself — he may unconsciously favor &quot;his own people&quot; (same clan, same lineage, same path cultivators), causing resources and opportunities to concentrate in a small circle. Heng Yuan Zhou prevents this with the following mechanisms:</p><ul><li><strong>Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision</strong>: the transcended one&#39;s resource-allocation records leave traces throughout; if systematic bias toward some clan or lineage appears, automatically trigger review;</li><li><strong>Rotation system</strong>: the transcended one periodically changes responsible region and post, avoiding staying in one place too long and forming a &quot;circle&quot;;</li><li><strong>Open review</strong>: mid-level cultivators&#39; promotion review involves multi-party representatives; the transcended one has only one vote;</li><li><strong>Appeal channel</strong>: unfairly treated mid-level cultivators may appeal to the Symbiotic Court.</li></ul><p>These mechanisms ensure the transcended one does not become a new &quot;sect master&quot; — turning middle cultivators into his private army.</p><h2 id="v-five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">V. Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: mid-level cultivators are civilization&#39;s largest talent pool; no harvest, no suppression is the greatest energy saving</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: cut the tower-top harvest-middle food chain, ensuring middle layer&#39;s labor fruits belong to the middle layer itself</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: in the Tang-Luo grace system, middle cultivators rise by grace; the ceiling is locked by Gu Chensha alone; in Heng Yuan Zhou the middle rises by more-work-more-pay, the ceiling is open to all</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: mid-level cultivators cover five Myriad-Rank lineages, impartial</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: promotion channels, review standards, and resource-allocation rules all open network-wide through the Selfless Dao</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Mid-level cultivators are civilization&#39;s waist. The transcended one&#39;s attitude toward the waist determines whether civilization is mobile or solidified. Heng Yuan Zhou requires the transcended one be an echelon builder, not a harvester, not a suppressor, not a circle boss. Waist hard, civilization stands straight. This is the orthodox definition of the transcended one&#39;s relationship with mid-level cultivators.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/36-社会结构与阶层流动.html">Entry 36 · Social Structure and Class Mobility</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/14-修炼境界统一划分.html">Entry 14 · Unified Cultivation-Realm Classification</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/22-资源分配联产承包机制.html">Entry 22 · Resource Allocation Household-Responsibility Mechanism</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/872_模块4-超脱者与社会-社会流动促进.html">Entry 872 · Transcended One&#39;s Promotion of Social Mobility</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',29)])])}const v=i(n,[["render",s]]);export{m as __pageData,v as default};
